+# AES differential research integration
+
+Prepared native integration; no scientific run has been executed in this repo.
+The nine cards in `hypotheses.json` are advisory proposals, not new backlog
+leases, official hypothesis records, accepted scientific results or authorizations.
+Convert executable follow-ups into the repository's ordinary `backlog/` cards
+before admitting their runs. The complete research assessment and nineteen
+primary-source receipts are in the companion autoresearcher study:
+https://github.com/aburan28/crypto-autoresearcher/tree/codex/aes-distinguisher-research/research/aes_open_angles_20261017
+
+The original frozen command card and 41-command observations are in
+`aburan28/cryptanalysis`, with source revision
+8a3ee1d85cbb32b0fb78aa8b92cc363e3e0caffd. Their results are not a new run here:
+https://github.com/aburan28/cryptanalysis/tree/codex/aes-distinguisher-research/experiments/aes-distinguisher-lab-20261017
+
+Before new execution, freeze this repository's source identity and a new exact
+protocol, use independent validation data and preserve source/binary/protocol
+hashes. New aggregate testing needs a frozen campaign alpha allocation.
+Nothing here changes the held official GOAL-AES-001/002/003 arms. The immediate
+obstruction is tracked in the companion access problem:
+https://github.com/aburan28/crypto-autoresearcher/blob/codex/aes-distinguisher-research/problems/aes-lab-conductor-and-campaign-admission.md
